  "referenceBehavior": "Pinned Iris creates shader objects, submits source, compiles, inspects status/logs, attaches/links programs, inspects link status/logs and manages shader destruction. It prebinds Minecraft attribute names and detaches stages after link.",
  "implementationScope": "Explicit owned snapshot -> existing include/macro/translation pipeline -> frozen caller-context GL API -> owned vertex/fragment program -> active interface reflection. Internal opt-in API only; no production installation.",
  "differences": "No Minecraft semantic prebinding is copied. Actual driver attribute/uniform locations and active output locations are validated. Attached stages are marked for deletion and retained by the owned program until its deletion, preserving existing attached-stage validation. This is not full Iris lifecycle or binding parity.",
  "contextContract": "native() only reads an already existing current GLFW context; no context/window creation or switching. Requires current owner thread and desktop GL >=4.3. CPU tests inject callbacks and identity only; identity equality is not a context-generation proof. Domain must outlive its leases, drain retirements and close on its own current context before teardown. Foreign-thread lease retirement performs no GL; owner collect deletes it. Uncollected final destruction on a foreign context never calls GL and increments a CPU diagnostic counter; this is a lifecycle-contract violation, not successful cleanup.",
  "resourceContract": "At most 8 occupied/reserved/retired program slots per domain, two attached stages per successful program or candidate. Candidate failures clean before replacement when context is valid; context loss retains bounded pending cleanup. Bound retired programs remain occupied until the caller unbinds them. No driver compiler time/memory bound or GPU-byte estimate is claimed. Existing frame/source/material/GPU budgets are unchanged.",
  "reflection": "Active attributes/uniforms must match declared names/types, have valid nonoverlapping locations, size one and bounded names/counts. Matrix attribute columns occupy separate slots. Optimized-away declarations remain inactive. Only vec4 output locations declared by the translator are accepted, with sparse indices unchanged; no colortex or physical attachment routes are inferred. Buffer blocks/SSBOs/atomic-counter buffers are rejected.",
  "limits": {
    "programSlots": 8,
    "stagesPerProgram": 2,
    "sourceBytesPerStage": 8388608,
    "sourcePathsPerStage": 4096,
    "logBytesPerStageOrProgram": 16384,
    "sourceLegendBytesPerStage": 16384,
    "activeAttributes": 16,
    "activeUniforms": 512,
    "activeNameBytes": 127,
    "activeOutputs": 8
  },
  "verification": "Pure CPU frozen-driver callbacks exercise exact sources, object ownership, status/log/reflection failures, replacement, capacity, moves, queued cleanup, context/thread checks, active/inactive resources and repeated releases. glslang compiles captured submitted source and independently reflects names/types, plus rejects a cross-stage mismatch. Neither represents real-driver reflection or image/FPS acceptance.",
  "javaExecuted": false,
  "clientsStarted": 0,
  "graphicsContextsCreated": 0,
  "accountsAccessed": false,
  "productionActivated": false,
  "irisContractComplete": false
